# Project Development Phase

## Project Title
Script-Controlled ACL: Restrict Record Access Based on Field Value

## Project Description
This project implements a ServiceNow Access Control List (ACL) using scripting to restrict record access based on a specific field value.

## Objective
The main objective is to control user access to records dynamically based on field-level conditions.

## Technologies Used
- ServiceNow
- ACL
- JavaScript
- Client Script
- UI Policy

## Key Features
- Restricts unauthorized record access.
- Uses script-based access control.
- Validates field values before allowing access.
- Improves data security in ServiceNow.

## Expected Outcome
The system allows users to access records only when the defined field conditions are satisfied.

## Conclusion
This project demonstrates how ServiceNow ACL scripting can be used to implement secure and condition-based record access.
